<title>TURKEY: Turk bourse sees 250,000 T cotton imports in 1997.</title>
<headline>Turk bourse sees 250,000 T cotton imports in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>IZMIR 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>An official from Turkey's leading Izmir commodity trade bourse said he expected cotton imports in the 1996/97 season to reach around 250,000 tonnes due to a domestic supply shortage which has pushed up prices.</p>
<p>&quot;Importers turned to Greece to buy cotton as prices brushed a high of 235,000 lira/kg on the bourse. Cotton imported from Greece costs 210,000 lira/kg... Cotton deliveries from Israel, Syria, Iran, Turkic republics, United States and North Africa also began,&quot; said Sadi Katrcoglu, vice-chairman of the Izmir trade bourse.</p>
</text>
